    <description>AuthGeek keeps your two-factor codes on your own computer rather than only on a phone.
Everything lives in one encrypted file on this machine: no account, no server, no sync.

* TOTP and HOTP, SHA1, SHA256 and SHA512, six to ten digits
* Add by pasting a link, by reading a QR code from a picture, or by typing it in
* Import everything from Google Authenticator's Transfer accounts QR in one go
* Show any account back as a QR code to add it to a phone
* Encrypted backup, plain text export and restore, all built in and tested
* Argon2id and AES-256-GCM, codes checked against the RFC test vectors on every build

Open source under GPL-3.0. The .NET 8 runtime is bundled, so there is nothing to install first.</description>
    <summary>Free offline two-factor authenticator for Windows, encrypted and on your own machine</summary>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/techygeekshome/AuthGeek/releases/tag/v1.0.0</releaseNotes>
